es we do  animation also we do entertainment news  so a breadth of different content that's  actually produced on new quinta dough  for us is mostly working with  independent studios as well as  independent directors and not  necessarily the very very large based TV  stations or establish production  companies those ones we actually also do  we call them joint productions and so  for the original content it's really  what we call what native is really born  from the web and design for the web  audience what's really significantly  different here is you look at the  audience of like an HBO or Netflix  they're actually quite similar because  internet penetration in us is so high  but in China internet only serves only  part of the audience whereas the  television audience maybe from five  years old all the way to 75 the instant  audience in the PC world went from about  18 to 35 and now with the mobile phone a  bit broader to 15 to 45 but still urban  young educated and very much an market  opportunity where you can provide  content for that specific audience in  contrast to the overall television  content that needs to address to a much  broader demographic  recently we've got a show caught on the  road which is a very interesting couple  who met each other over 20 years ago in  high school and started a company  together selling tofu machines and they  sold the company after they were  actually went to volunteer at a citron  earthquake and realized that life is  short they sold the company and they  started traveling all around the world  in some of the most adventurous places  places like weather Chernobyl nuclear  plant Somalia where Black Hawk Down was  filmed and so forth and the fella in the  show his nickname to cemani because it's  a pre heavyset guy basically a promise  his girlfriend at the time very very  unique wedding so towards the end of the  first season actually proposed her in  the North Pole and in the second season  the collarbone and traveled fro